From f6f6a0d8fdb5ff90858c2da9eb96374ab295ad93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grafici patch export <patch-export@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:48:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix spline workspace bounds and unclipped autoscaling

Fix both spline correctness findings in one patch against origin/main 575ef29.
Apply this patch before the rebased patches/float16.patch. No separate
spline-bounds or spline-autoscale patch is needed.

Allocate n+1 complete floats for l/u/z rather than sizeof(float)*n+1 bytes.
Reject unsupported source/output counts, guard knot-pair reads and release
all partial allocations on failure. Correct temporary solver payload is
20*n+12 bytes, n=source_count-1; retained coefficient arrays do not grow.

Discover the output range from unclipped cubic evaluations before creating
DataNorm samples. Reuse a constant-size Horner evaluator for sampling and
range discovery. AUTOSCALE=false retains explicit source-range clipping.
Autoscaling covers emitted samples, not extrema between output samples.

Validation: guarded allocations, all five injected allocation failures,
capacity/empty-input boundaries and cubic-overshoot regressions pass with
C++11, UBSan and float-cast-overflow. The following precision patch extends
the same regressions to Float16 without reintroducing either fix.
